---
import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/gujarati-font-converter"
  lede="Planned: a Gujarati font converter for legacy Gujarati DTP fonts to Unicode Gujarati."
>
  <h2>Planned, not started</h2>
  <p>
    Gujarati uses its own script, not Devanagari. That means none of the current
    character maps apply and none of the Devanagari-specific reordering rules do
    either. A Gujarati converter is a new map and a new set of rules, not an
    extra table bolted onto this one.
  </p>
  <p>
    The route exists so the work has somewhere to land. It will be switched on
    only after a keyword check and a mapping tested against real Gujarati
    documents. See <a href="/all-converters">all converters</a> for what is
    working today.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
